From c7b61e655917741d52dd4aae2b7a686657a02c79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Liberty <mliberty@precisioninno.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:10:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] python: make the openroad wheel installable and add
 Python unit tests

The wheel kept repository paths (python/openroad/, src/odb/odb.py), so
`import openroad` failed after `pip install`, and the per-tool modules the
tests import (odb, utl, ant, grt, ...) existed only as shims that
test/bazel_test.sh wrote at test time.

- python/modules holds the per-tool modules as files. openroadpy depends
  on them, the wheel installs them and the openroad package at the top
  level, and bazel_test.sh puts them on the path instead of writing shims.
- odb_py, utl_py and gpl_py no longer add their source directories to
  sys.path. A py_test's `import odb` had loaded a second copy of the
  module next to the src.odb.odb that openroadpy uses, so isinstance
  failed across the two.
- Hermetic py_test examples: openroad_test (unittest) and wheel_test,
  which installs the wheel into an empty directory and imports it in an
  isolated interpreter.

Signed-off-by: Matt Liberty <mliberty@precisioninno.com>
