diff --git a/docs/agents/testing.md b/docs/agents/testing.md
index 3386d77847..b0d4d0fbf2 100644
--- a/docs/agents/testing.md
+++ b/docs/agents/testing.md
@@ -87,3 +87,32 @@ Unit tests are C++ files located at `src/<module>/test/cpp`.
 ### Test Registration
 - CMake: `src/<module>/test/CMakeLists.txt`
 - Bazel: `src/<module>/test/BUILD` or `src/<module>/test/cpp/BUILD`
+
+## Python Unit Tests
+
+Python binding tests can be plain `unittest` modules run as Bazel `py_test`
+targets on the hermetic interpreter, one test method per behavior. The
+example is `python/openroad/openroad_test.py`:
+
+```python
+load("@rules_python//python:defs.bzl", "py_test")
+
+py_test(
+    name = "openroad_test",
+    size = "small",
+    srcs = ["openroad_test.py"],
+    deps = ["//python/openroad:openroadpy"],
+)
+```
+
+`//python/openroad:openroadpy` provides `import openroad` and the per-tool
+modules (`import odb`, `import ant`, ...) from `python/modules`, the same
+names the wheel installs. Keep each `Tech` alive while its `Design` or the
+module-level functions (`set_thread_count`, ...) are in use.
+
+### The openroad wheel
+
+`bazelisk build //python/openroad:openroad_wheel` builds an abi3 wheel (CPython
+3.10 or later) that installs into any virtualenv with `pip install`.
+`//python/openroad:wheel_test` checks that it imports in a fresh interpreter
+without the Bazel runfiles.
diff --git a/python/modules/BUILD b/python/modules/BUILD
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..69e13aea2c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/python/modules/BUILD
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
+# Copyright (c) 2026, The OpenROAD Authors
+
+load("@rules_python//python:defs.bzl", "py_library")
+
+package(features = ["layering_check"])
+
+# Top-level per-tool modules (import odb, import ant, ...), matching the
+# modules `openroad -python` provides. They re-export the extension
+# modules, so //python/openroad:openroadpy depends on this target and the
+# wheel installs these files at the top level.
+py_library(
+    name = "modules",
+    srcs = glob(["*.py"]),
+    imports = ["."],
+    visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
+)
